{"version":1,"kind":"summary","errors":27,"warnings":0,"explanations":{"E0032":"# E0032: value of the wrong type\n\nA value must have the type its position expects: the declared type of a `let`, the parameter of a function, the return type of a function, the operand of an operator.\n\n## Why\n\nSisu does not convert between number types by itself. A `u8`, a `char`, an `i64` and an `f64` are different types even when the number would fit, so a program says where one becomes another with `u8(...)`, `i64(...)`, `f64(...)` or `char(...)`. A `u8` and a `char` convert through `i64`: `char(i64(b))`, and `f64(i64(b))`. A conversion takes one type: `i64(...)` takes a `u8`, a `char` or an `f64`, and `u8(...)`, `char(...)` and `f64(...)` take an `i64`. An `i64` beside an `f64` in arithmetic or a comparison, as in `n * x`, is the one reported, with the unsafe fix to convert it: `f64(n) * x`. Where the context wants an `i64`, as `n += x` does, the `f64` is the one reported, and no fix converts it. A value that does not fit makes `u8(...)` or `char(...)` fail, and an `f64` that is not a whole number in `i64`'s range makes `i64(...)` fail, so each gives an optional, a `u8?`, a `char?` or an `i64?`: give a default with `??`, or unwrap it with `if let`. The fix that converts is offered only where that optional is expected.\n\nA value converts to an optional through one `?` only: `let x: i64? = 5` is valid, but `let x: i64?? = 5` is not. Wrap the value in `Some(...)` for each further layer: `let x: i64?? = Some(5)`.\n\nA value converts to an interface value, `any Shape`, when its type conforms to `Shape` and it is not an optional. An `i64?` is no `any Display`, and a `Circle?` is no `any Shape` and no `(any Shape)?`. Unwrap the optional with `if let` or `??`, then convert the value. A `Circle` converts to `(any Shape)?` and is wrapped.\n\nA `panic` or `todo` message is a `string`. An `i64`, `u8`, `f64`, `bool` or `char` written on one line becomes one with interpolation: `panic(n)` is `panic(\"{n}\")`, and `todo(n)` is `todo(\"{n}\")`.\n\n## Broken\n\n```sisu\nfn main() {\n    let n: i64 = 5\n    let b: u8 = n\n    print(b)\n}\n```\n\n## Fixed\n\n```sisu\nfn main() {\n    let n: i64 = 5\n    let b: u8 = u8(n) ?? 0\n    print(b)\n}\n```\n"}}
